# This tape neither rings the bell at the end of a pass nor halts on an error.
# It prints its banner once and then one line per pass,
#
#	END PASS #     1  TOTAL ERRORS SINCE LAST REPORT      0
#
# with the failed tests listed above it. So the end of a pass is the text, and
# "no errors" is the count in it - which is why the pass text reaches into the
# number instead of stopping at "END PASS": that alone would pass the tape with
# its errors still being printed. A count of ten or more reads "     10" and
# does not match.
pass-text = TOTAL ERRORS SINCE LAST REPORT      0
